cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Hephaestus in your research, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: Hephaestus
abstract: >-
  Hephaestus is an open-source AI mentor for software engineering practices. It reads pull
  requests, merge requests, issues and code reviews where they happen, and checks them against the
  practices that a team chose. When a review finds a problem it can support, Hephaestus can point to the work,
  explain what to improve, and suggest a next step. An observation can say when the evidence
  could not settle a question. Developers can talk the feedback through in a conversation.
authors:
  - name: TUM Applied Education Technologies
    website: https://aet.cit.tum.de/
repository-code: https://github.com/hephaestus-build/Hephaestus
url: https://hephaestus.build
license: MIT
keywords:
  - ai-mentor
  - practice-feedback
  - engineering-practices
  - developer-feedback
  - self-hosted
